+# Frontend remediation test report
+
+## Batch 1 review follow-up — authentication/session reliability
+
+### Executed checks
+
+- [x] `node --test tests/*.test.mjs` — **passed: 21 tests, 0 failures, exit 0**. Includes the 12 prior auth/session tests plus API transport integration for CSRF bootstrap/header, cookie credentials, login CSRF reacquisition, refresh probe/rotation/retry, 401 handling, transient failures, multipart, late 401, concurrent calls and no-Web-Locks fail-closed behavior.
+- [x] `npm run lint` — **passed, exit 0**. The custom TypeScript-AST source guard checked 74 TypeScript files for debugger statements, explicit `any`, console logging and TypeScript suppression directives. It is not ESLint and does not claim full style/rule coverage.
+- [x] JSON parsing of `package.json` and `vercel.json` — passed in prior run.
+- [ ] `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund --fetch-retries=0 --fetch-timeout=20000` — **failed, exit 1**. npm 10.9.2 emitted `Exit handler never called!`; prior run recorded `EAI_AGAIN` resolving `registry.npmjs.org`. Offline install also failed with `ENOTCACHED` for `zwitch@2.0.4`. The dependency tree is incomplete.
+- [ ] `npm run typecheck` — **failed, exit 2**: `TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for 'vite/client'`. This is an environment/dependency failure; no semantic typecheck pass is claimed.
+- [ ] `npm run build` — **failed, exit 2** at the same TypeScript prerequisite; Vite production bundling did not start.
+- [ ] GitHub Actions — workflow added but not executed. No repository remote/CI credentials or connected CI runner are available in this workspace.
+- [ ] Real-browser/backend tests — **not run**. No live Django endpoint or browser automation environment was provided.
+
+### API transport test boundary
+
+`tests/api-client.test.mjs` imports and exercises the same `src/lib/api-client.mjs` module bound by the production `src/lib/api.ts`. It uses a deterministic fake fetch transport and simulated Web Locks. It verifies request construction and refresh state transitions, but does not test an actual browser cookie jar, CORS, Django middleware, Paystack, or concurrent real HTTP requests.
+
+### Backend contract verification
+
+Reviewed the backend source export:
+
+- `apps/users/views.py`: `CsrfCookieView`, `RegisterView`, `LoginView`, `CookieTokenRefreshView`, `LogoutView`.
+- `apps/users/cookies.py`: HttpOnly access/refresh cookies; refresh cookie path `/api/auth/`.
+- `apps/users/urls.py`: `csrf/`, `register/`, `login/`, `logout/`, `token/refresh/`, `me/` routes.
+
+`LoginView` and `RegisterView` use `csrf_protect` and set auth cookies, but do not call `django.contrib.auth.login()` or `rotate_token()`. The CSRF endpoint returns a masked token using `get_token()`. Frontend still clears/reacquires after successful login/register.
+
+`CookieTokenRefreshView` catches invalid/blacklisted refresh tokens and checks the access cookie from that same request. If that access cookie remains valid, it returns 200 without issuing new cookies. If access is expired/invalid, it clears auth cookies and returns 401. This fallback does not guarantee safe simultaneous refresh when Web Locks are unavailable and access has expired.
+
+### Limitations
+
+The API-client suite exercises the production transport module using a fake fetch implementation and simulated Web Locks. It does not exercise real browser cookie jars, cross-origin CORS, Django middleware, or actual concurrent HTTP requests. Typecheck and production build remain unverified. Browsers without Web Locks fail closed and require reauthentication after expiry; broad release to those browsers is not approved without a backend coordination change. TV-FE-002 remains blocked pending the actual API hostname and hosting rewrite configuration.
